Base relocations of ReadyToRun code on witos (plan step S8.2): ApplyBaseRelocations opens an executable section for
writing with PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE on every Unix but Apple's ARM64, which WitOS never grants (writable and executable
at once); the arm64 SDK's images carry relocations in their code and load elsewhere than their preferred base, so
NuGet.Versioning failed to load with ERROR_INVALID_ACCESS (C2.5 on ARM64). On witos the section stays writable alone
while the relocations are written, and the restore to the section's protection, which the libc publishes, follows.

--- a/src/coreclr/vm/peimagelayout.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/vm/peimagelayout.cpp
@@ -300,6 +300,9 @@
 #if defined(__APPLE__) && defined(HOST_ARM64)
                     // Enable writing on Apple Silicon
                     PAL_JitWriteProtect(true);
+#elif defined(TARGET_WITOS)
+                    // WitOS never grants writable and executable at once: the section is written through a writable
+                    // window and the restore below gives it its protection again, which the libc publishes.
 #else
                     // On SELinux, we cannot change protection that doesn't have execute access rights
                     // to one that has it, so we need to set the protection to RWX instead of RW
